{title: Lord, Reign in Me (FJ_111_en)}
{subtitle: Über alle Welt}
{song_number: 111}
{language: en}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{key: C}
{composer: Brenton Brown}
{lyricist: Brenton Brown}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C]Over all the [Gsus4]earth, You [F]reign on [Gsus4]high,
[C]every moun[Gsus4]tain stream, every [F]sunset [Gsus4]sky.
[Am7]But my one re[Gsus4]quest, [F]Lord, my only [Gsus4]aim
[Dm7]is that You'd [F]reign in [Gsus4]me a[C]gain.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C]Over every [Gsus4]thought, [F]over every [Gsus4]word,
[C]may my life re[Gsus4]flect the [F]beauty of my [Gsus4]Lord;
[Am7]'cause You mean [Gsus4]more to me [F]than any earthly [Gsus4]thing.
[Dm7]So won't You [F]reign in [Gsus4]me a[C]gain.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C]Lord, reign in [G]me, [F]reign in Your [G]pow'r;
[C]over all my [G]dreams, [F]in my darkest [G]hour.
[Am]You are the [G]Lord [F]of all I [G]am,
[Dm7]so won't You [F]reign in [G]me a[C]gain.
{end_of_chorus}
